  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile + avgpool with PCA (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms singleprofile PCA (config_001, acc=0.485), indicating that multi-profile aggregation is a critical design axis. The natural next question is whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further improve on avgpool within the same multiprofile+PCA setup. config_003 is a clean single-variable change (avgpool → transformer) from the best result, so any performance difference can be attributed to the aggregation method. This is the best use of the next budget slot because it either confirms avgpool sufficiency (freeing us to explore other dimensions like multimodal fusion or alternative encoders) or reveals a further gain that justifies committing to transformer-based aggregation in subsequent multimodal experiments. Testing multimodal fusion now would be premature given the very weak image-only signal (config_010, acc=0.208), and testing alternative RNA encoders in multiprofile is lower priority since PCA already dominates scgpt in singleprofile."
}

